+3. **Candidate Collapsibles & Viewport Wrapping:** Every candidate considered during resolution is presented in a keyboard-accessible Textual `Collapsible` widget in deterministic resolution order. The candidate corresponding to the selected installation (matching the opening installation key) is initially expanded by default, while shadowed or alternate candidates remain collapsed. Candidate titles and content wrap cleanly without horizontal overflow at terminal dimensions 100x30 and 60x24. The screen body is laid out in a coherent vertical scroll container (`#why-body`), ensuring that candidate collapsibles and their details (canonical/entrypoint paths, hash, reason, rule, evidence, and notes) remain readable with candidates container height >= 4, and reachable via keyboard navigation (PageDown/PageUp/Tab/Enter).
